  "worked_solution": "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{23}=-2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 0 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 0 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
